  "title": "What Happens When The Work Number Can't Verify Your Applicant?",
  "summary": "The Work Number covers only about 40% of U.S. employers, so 'no record found' is a routine result — not an edge case. This is the structured fallback waterfall that completes verification when TWN comes up empty: written VOE, borrower-assisted payroll connection, multi-channel manual outreach, and human escalation.",
